// Keyless type for the no-key endpoint-kinds interop proof.
//
// No @key member => Connext registers NO_KEY DataWriter/DataReader endpoints
// (RTPS 2.5 §9.3.1.2: writer kind 0x03, reader kind 0x04), the foreign-side
// counterpart to this stack's nokey-data (define-dds-type with no :key member,
// type-support-keyed-p NIL). The two interop round-trips prove a no-key type
// crosses the wire both directions; a no-key endpoint here will NOT match a
// keyed (WITH_KEY 0x02/0x07) endpoint — that is the silent non-match guard.
//
// @final to match this stack's :final extensibility; two 32-bit longs, member
// ids 0,1 via default @autoid(SEQUENTIAL). The registered type name is set to
// "nokey-data" at the Topic constructor (3-arg overload) so it is byte-identical
// to our registered type-name; discovery matches on topic name + type name.

@final
struct NoKeyData {
    long a;
    long b;
};
